<section id="technical-connections" aria-label="Technical connections">
 <div class="pipeline-technical"><div class="section-head panel-heading"><div><p class="label">TWO TECHNICAL CONNECTIONS</p><h3>Where human judgments enter model development.</h3></div></div><div class="two-grid"><article><span class="label">POST-TRAINING</span><h3>Demonstrations and preferences play different roles.</h3><p>Supervised fine-tuning can learn from examples of desired responses. In a common RLHF approach, comparisons inform a reward model used for reinforcement learning. DPO offers a way to optimize from preferences without a separate reward-model training stage.</p><p>The data must match its purpose: a policy compliance label, a preferred response and a demonstration are different artifacts.</p><footer><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.02155" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">InstructGPT paper ↗</a><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.18290" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DPO paper ↗</a></footer></article><article><span class="label">CONTINUOUS EVALUATION</span><h3>Check what changed and what broke.</h3><p>Maintain versioned test cases, prompts and grading criteria. Compare model versions, inspect failures and preserve known cases in a regression suite. Keep evaluation holdouts separate from training data to reduce leakage.</p><p>A new failure can inform later evaluation coverage or training work after review. A score alone does not identify whether the model, environment or grader caused the problem.</p><footer><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/demystifying-evals-for-ai-agents" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Anthropic · evaluation structure & regression ↗</a></footer></article></div></div>
 <footer class="library-references"><p class="label">REFERENCE READING</p><a href="https://labelstud.io/tutorials/how_to_measure_inter_annotator_agreement_and_build_human_consensus" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Label Studio · agreement & consensus ↗</a><a href="https://aclanthology.org/J08-4004/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Artstein &amp; Poesio · agreement measures ↗</a><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/demystifying-evals-for-ai-agents" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Anthropic · evaluation concepts ↗</a><p>Examples here are illustrative study notes. Project terminology, label definitions and acceptance rules should be confirmed with the team.</p></footer>
